# The Barista — Privacy Policy

**Effective date:** November 5, 2026
**Developer:** AxiomaraGames
**Contact:** axiomaragames@gmail.com

The Barista ("the app") is a coffee encyclopedia: coffee drinks, brewing methods, beans and origins, and guides. This policy explains what information the app handles, and the licence of the software it is built with.

## Summary

The app does not collect, transmit, sell or share any personal data. Everything you choose in it stays on your device.

## Information the app stores on your device

To work, the app saves the following, **only on your device**:

- **Favorites:** the drinks, brewing methods and beans you save
- **Recently viewed:** the pages you opened last
- **Make with What You Have:** the ingredients and equipment you selected
- **Settings:** your language and your choice of units (ml or oz)

This information is never sent to us or to anyone else. It is deleted when you uninstall the app or clear its data in your device's settings.

**Device backups:** if you have turned on Android's backup feature, Android may include the app's data in your device backup, stored in your Google account under Google's own privacy terms. We have no access to these backups.

**Sharing a recipe:** when you use Share on a drink, the recipe's text is copied to your device's clipboard. Nothing is sent anywhere unless you paste it yourself.

## What the app does not do

- It does not ask you to create an account or sign in.
- It does not connect to the internet. All drinks, methods, beans, guides and their photos are built into the app.
- It does not collect analytics, crash reports, location, contacts or device identifiers.
- It does not show ads and contains no advertising or tracking software.
- It does not use your camera, microphone or files.

## Children

The app is a general reference about coffee and is not directed at children. We do not knowingly collect information from anyone, including children, because we collect no information at all.

## Changes to this policy

If this policy changes, the new version will be published at this address with a new effective date. Because the app collects no data, any change will not affect information you have already given us.

